"/w/images/7/70/Search_icon.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></a></span></span> <details class=\"bg3wiki-uid\">\n<summary>UUID</summary>\n<code class=\"bg3wiki-uid-box\">2eabd463-e5f3-41a2-ad6f-adffa400fa03</code>\n</details> <span class=\"bg3wiki-uid-link\"><span class=\"mw-default-size bg3wiki-icon\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=uuid:2eabd463-e5f3-41a2-ad6f-adffa400fa03\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\"><img alt=\"https://bg3.norbyte.dev/search?q=uuid:2eabd463-e5f3-41a2-ad6f-adffa400fa03\" src=\"/w/images/7/70/Search_icon.svg\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\"></a></span></span></li></ul>\n</div>   \n<div style=\"clear: both;\"></div></div>\n    <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Where_to_find\"> Where to find </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-tooltip-box\">\n<ul><li>In the <a href=\"/wiki/Stormshore_Tabernacle\" title=\"Stormshore Tabernacle\">Stormshore Tabernacle</a> at <span class=\"bg3wiki-coordinates\">X:&nbsp;115&nbsp;Y:&nbsp;-30</span></li></ul>\n</div>  <h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Text\"> Text </span></h2>\n<div class=\"bg3wiki-book-text\">\n<p>...thus I wonder whether the following thesis might hold water: That as city life becomes more precarious, as the marching armies menace the borders, that people will turn not to the gods who allowed this to happen, but to the dark entities who might have the power to stop it. I speak of the Dead Three: <a href=\"/wiki/Bane_(deity)\" title=\"Bane (deity)\">Bane</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Bhaal\" title=\"Bhaal\">Bhaal</a>, and <a href=\"/wiki/Myrkul\" title=\"Myrkul\">Myrkul</a>. For when death threatens your door, who better than the god of living death to protect you? Is it not better to murder than be murdered? And through domination in its purest form, is not the dominator protected? I predict, then, that the coming days will see a wave of conversion such as we have never seen before.\n</p>\n</div>    \n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20260714212155\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [vary‐revision‐sha1, no‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.048 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.050 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 1332/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 25497/4194304 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 7756/4194304 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 22/200\nExpensive parser function count: 1/750\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2/5000000 bytes\nExtLoops count: 0/1000\nLua time usage: 0.011/7.000 seconds\nLua memory usage: 935769/52428800 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   41.045      1 Template:MiscItemPage\n100.00%   41.045      1 -total\n 48.93%   20.083      6 Template:Icon_text\n 43.55%   17.876     15 Template:Trim\n 22.73%    9.329      2 Template:Uid\n 17.13%    7.032      1 Template:Main_only\n 13.16%    5.403      2 Template:Template_style\n 10.67%    4.381      6 Template:Ifempty\n 10.65%    4.373      1 Template:PageSeo\n 10.52%    4.319      1 Template:Notes\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key bg3wiki:pcache:idhash:31365-0!canonical and timestamp 20260714212155 and revision id 394537. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}